# build_styles.py imports pickers / implementation / themes, so running the
# generator leaves bytecode behind. Nothing here ships.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Excel lock files
~$*

# Runtime state, written by start_dashboard.sh and the bake. Nothing here is
# source: logs, pidfiles, the live sleeve library and the proposal register.
# None of it travels: the host seeds its own library and starts with an empty
# register, and a copied .db would carry my rows into it.
#
# var/baked IS tracked, and deliberately. It is a DELIVERY, not a cache: the
# host computes no analytics, so those 16 slices and their manifest are the
# figures every proposal is made of, and the Cyrus checkout is on another
# machine with git as the way across. Rebuild with
#   python3 -m cyrus_pmg.pmgService.scenario.bake --all
# or, with no database, --adapter fixtures.
service/var/*
!service/var/baked/

# The IMF WEO release download writes an empty file relative to the working
# directory before falling back to the vendored copy (D11). Nothing reads it.
service/weo_2026_1.csv
